msgid "Start by running the 5-step Security Setup Wizard on the Dashboard. It turns on high-value, zero-friction protections (Login Limiter, Honeypots, Basic Firewall, Security Headers) while leaving disruptive options (Country Blocking, Site Password, Hide Login URL, HSTS, and AI Crawler Blocker) OFF until you deliberately choose them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:128
msgid "Go to WPEPP Security → Dashboard to view your live Security Score ring (0–100, Grade A–F) and 30-day event counters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:129
msgid "Click Run Setup Wizard to apply safe baseline rules step-by-step without accidentally locking yourself out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:130
msgid "If your site runs behind Cloudflare or a reverse proxy, visit Block Center → IP Lists immediately and add Trusted Proxies before turning on strict IP lockouts or Country Restriction."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:131
msgid "Open the Site Health Audit Report modal from the Dashboard to see exact failing checks and jump straight to each setting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:132
msgid "Use the Dark/Light theme toggle in the top header bar anytime for comfortable admin reading."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:136
msgid "Security Score & Checklist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:138
msgid "Always Active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:139
msgid "Tracks weighted security controls across Firewall, Login Protection, Hardening, Scanner, and Anti-Spam. Local development hosts (localhost / .test / .local) are detected automatically so non-HTTPS local sites are not unfairly penalized."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:140
msgid "Do not blindly enable advanced restrictions like HSTS Preload, Site Access Gate, or AI Crawler Blocker just to chase a higher score—only enable controls that match your real site requirements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:143
msgid "Security Setup Wizard (5 Steps)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:145
#: includes/class-docs.php:152
#: includes/class-docs.php:204
#: includes/class-docs.php:357
#: includes/class-docs.php:896
msgid "On-Demand"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:146
msgid "Configures safe core defaults sequentially (login brute-force limiter, honeypots, spam shield, firewall basics, and recommended hardening) with a one-click Skip option per step."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:147
msgid "Do not skip reviewing Block Center → IP Lists afterward if your site uses Cloudflare—proxy headers must be trusted for accurate attacker IP logging."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:150
msgid "1-Click Site Health Audit Report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:153
msgid "Generates a scannable summary inside the Dashboard showing passed checks, open risks, and direct links to fix each item."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:154
msgid "Avoid running audit checks right before putting a site in Maintenance Mode—do audits in normal live/staging state for accurate header results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:168
msgid "Web Application Firewall (WAF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:170
msgid "WPEPP Security → Firewall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:172
msgid "Inspects incoming HTTP requests for SQL injection (SQLi), Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), path traversal, wp-config.php probing, and malicious bots before they can exploit WordPress or your plugins."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:174
msgid "Enable Firewall (Basic Mode) to immediately filter suspicious requests inside WordPress initialization."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:175
msgid "On complex stores or custom headless apps, enable Learning Mode for 24–72 hours first to watch the Recent Matches log without blocking real visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:176
msgid "Pro users can switch on Extended Protection (Early Boot) once host compatibility is confirmed for maximum pre-WordPress blocking speed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:180
msgid "Firewall Enabled (Basic Mode)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:182
msgid "Off / Wizard Opt-In"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:183
msgid "Enforces all built-in WAF inspection rules during WordPress runtime. Works reliably on every shared host, VPS, Apache, LiteSpeed, and Nginx server without server config changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:184
msgid "After enabling, quickly test complex page-builder saves (Elementor/Bricks) or custom code-snippet plugins—HTML/script payloads in POST fields can occasionally look like XSS if Learning Mode was skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:187
msgid "Learning Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:190
msgid "Evaluates all WAF rules and records matching requests inside Recent Matches without returning a 403 block. Ideal for auditing WooCommerce webhooks, REST integrations, or API tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:191
msgid "Do NOT leave Learning Mode turned on permanently in production! While Learning Mode is active, attacks are only logged—they are not blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:194
msgid "Extended Protection (Early-Boot Mode)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:198
msgid "Configures PHP auto_prepend_file via .user.ini or .htaccess so attacks are rejected before WordPress core, database connections, or plugins load—saving CPU and memory under attack. Built-in auto-failsafe disables bootstrap if PHP fails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:199
msgid "Do NOT enable without a fresh host backup on hosts that strictly lock .user.ini or disallow php_value in .htaccess. On pure Nginx + PHP-FPM without .user.ini support, configure auto_prepend_file at the pool level or stay on Basic Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:202
msgid "Live Rule Tester & Recent Matches"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:205
msgid "Simulate any URL path, HTTP method (GET/POST), User-Agent, and POST body in the Rule Tester to see which rule triggers and why. Review Recent Matches for matched rule ID, severity, and client IP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:206
msgid "Do not test live production URLs by sending real attack strings from your own admin IP if auto-blocking/lockouts are active unless your office IP is on the IP Allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:220
msgid "Malware & Integrity Scanner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:222
msgid "WPEPP Security → Scanner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:224
msgid "Scans your WordPress installation in non-blocking slices across 4 stages: Suspicious Files & Malware Signatures, WordPress Core Checksums, Database Options Injection, and Admin/User Role Integrity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:228
msgid "Verify Before Clicking \"Delete File\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:229
msgid "Heuristic rules can occasionally flag legitimate obfuscated third-party files, licensed themes, or cache helpers. Deleting a core theme or WooCommerce file directly can crash your site (WSOD). Always inspect the file path and snippet first, take a backup, and reinstall affected plugins from wordpress.org when confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:233
msgid "Click Quick Scan for a fast baseline check on active code, core checksums, options, and users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:234
msgid "Run Full Scan weekly (or immediately after any suspected breach) to inspect deeper directories and uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:235
msgid "Review any flagged findings carefully—use Ignore for verified false positives, Resolve once cleaned, or Delete only on confirmed stray/backdoor files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:239
msgid "Quick Scan vs. Full Scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:241
msgid "Manual Trigger"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:242
msgid "Quick Scan checks high-risk directories, core file checksums against official WordPress hashes, critical database options, and rogue admin users. Full Scan adds exhaustive traversal across plugin/theme/upload directories."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:243
msgid "Avoid running Full Scan repeatedly on shared hosting with massive 50,000+ file media libraries during peak traffic—run Quick Scan daily and schedule Full Scan during off-peak hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:246
msgid "Finding Actions (Resolve / Ignore / Delete)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:248
msgid "Per Finding"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:249
msgid "Read the built-in Fix Recommendation first. Click Ignore if you personally authored or verified the code; click Resolve after replacing an infected plugin from a clean source."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:250
msgid "Never click Delete on wp-config.php, active theme functions.php, or core files—removing those takes the site offline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:253
msgid "Daily Automatic Scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:256
msgid "Automatically runs background scan slices every 24 hours via WP-Cron and sends email alerts if critical malware or core tampering appears."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:257
msgid "Do not rely on scheduled scans if DISABLE_WP_CRON is set to true without a real server-side crontab calling wp-cron.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:260
msgid "Antivirus Definition Database & Signature Sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:262
msgid "Built-In Rules Active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:263
msgid "Displays total active malware signatures and lets you sync fresh signatures on demand. Built-in signatures stay active even if your host blocks outbound feed requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:264
msgid "You do not need to click Sync before every manual scan—local rules work immediately offline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:278
#: build/247.js:1
#: src/pages/Security/AntiSpam.jsx:99
msgid "Anti-Spam & Bot Shield"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:280
msgid "WPEPP Security → Anti-Spam"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:282
msgid "Multi-layer bot defense covering WooCommerce registration, WordPress comments, login, and password-reset forms using zero-friction honeypots, timing checks, rate limiters, disposable email filtering, and CAPTCHA challenges."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:284
msgid "Keep the Master Anti-Spam Shield toggle ON—all safe honeypot defaults run silently with zero UX friction for humans."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:285
msgid "Filter by category pills (WooCommerce Shield, Comment Spam, Login & Forms, CAPTCHA Engine) to fine-tune specific forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:286
msgid "In Pro, configure Cloudflare Turnstile or Google reCAPTCHA keys inside Universal CAPTCHA Engine and test with Test Mode ON before enforcing hard blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:290
msgid "WooCommerce Registration Honeypot & Rate Limiter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:293
msgid "Adds an invisible honeypot field to WooCommerce account/checkout signups and caps rapid signups from a single IP so fake customer floods are stopped automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:294
msgid "If customers register from shared corporate/school Wi-Fi or behind unconfigured Cloudflare proxies, configure Block Center → Trusted Proxies first so legitimate users do not share one rate-limit bucket."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:297
#: build/247.js:1
#: src/pages/Security/AntiSpam.jsx:182
msgid "Block Disposable & Temp Emails on WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:299
msgid "On (Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:300
msgid "Rejects customer signups from 200+ temporary/burner inbox providers (Mailinator, Guerrilla Mail, YOPmail, etc.) to stop coupon abuse and fake accounts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:301
msgid "Temporarily disable if your QA team tests WooCommerce checkout with Mailinator/temp email addresses, or if privacy-focused buyers intentionally use burner aliases."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:304
msgid "Comment Form Honeypot & <3s Time-Gate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:307
msgid "Pairs an invisible trap field with a sub-3-second submission timer—human commenters take longer than 3 seconds to read and type, whereas automated spam scripts submit in milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:308
msgid "Turn off Time-Gate if a heavily customized AJAX comment plugin submits without printing the hidden timestamp field."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:311
msgid "Login & Lost Password Honeypots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:314
msgid "Traps automated credential-stuffing and password-reset flooding bots with invisible inputs on wp-login.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:315
msgid "Safe for almost every site; only check compatibility if an aggressive browser extension auto-fills hidden non-standard fields."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:318
msgid "Universal CAPTCHA Engine (Turnstile / reCAPTCHA v2 & v3)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:321
msgid "Choose Cloudflare Turnstile (recommended, frictionless), Google reCAPTCHA v2 (checkbox), or v3 (invisible 0.1–0.9 score threshold, default 0.5). Once keys are saved, enable CAPTCHA independently on Login, Registration, WooCommerce, Comments, or Lost Password."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:322
msgid "NEVER set reCAPTCHA v3 threshold too high (0.8–0.9) right away—privacy browsers and VPN users score lower and get blocked. Always enable CAPTCHA Test Mode (Do not block submissions) while verifying your keys!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:336
msgid "Block Center & IP Lists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:338
msgid "WPEPP Security → Block Center"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:340
msgid "Central control hub for inspecting automatic lockouts/404-flood bans, issuing manual IP/CIDR blocks, configuring Cloudflare/reverse proxy trust headers, and maintaining permanent IP Blocklists & Allowlists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:344
msgid "Using Cloudflare, Load Balancers, or Nginx Proxy? Set Trusted Proxies First!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:345
msgid "To prevent IP header spoofing, WPEPP only trusts X-Forwarded-For or CF-Connecting-IP when the direct peer (REMOTE_ADDR) is listed in Trusted Reverse Proxies. On Cloudflare sites, click \"1-Click Add Cloudflare IP Ranges\" inside IP Lists so attacks and Country Restrictions resolve the visitor's true IP instead of locking everyone behind one Cloudflare edge IP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:349
msgid "Visit Block Center → Blocks to review active temporary or permanent bans (shows type: Manual, Auto 404 flood, Rate limit, Login lockout, Country)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:350
msgid "To ban an attacker immediately, enter a single IP or CIDR range (e.g. 203.0.113.0/24), pick duration (1 hour, 24 hours, 7 days, Permanent), add an optional reason, and click Add Block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:351
msgid "Open IP Lists to inspect your live REMOTE_ADDR vs. Resolved Client IP, configure Cloudflare/Proxy ranges, and maintain Pro Blocklists/Allowlists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:355
msgid "Manual IP / CIDR Blocks & Purge Expired"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:358
msgid "Block single IPs or subnet ranges temporarily (1h/24h/7d) or permanently, track hit counts per rule, and click Purge expired blocks anytime to tidy old bans."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:359
msgid "Never enter massive ranges like /8 or /16 without verifying WHOIS ownership, and always check Your IP in IP Lists so you do not ban your own network."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:362
msgid "Reverse Proxy & 1-Click Cloudflare IP Ranges"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:364
msgid "Direct REMOTE_ADDR Only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:365
msgid "Automatically detects Cloudflare traffic and populates official Cloudflare CIDRs into Trusted Reverse Proxies in one click (click Save Changes afterward to persist)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:366
msgid "Do NOT add arbitrary public IPs or 0.0.0.0/0 to Trusted Proxies—doing so lets any attacker forge fake X-Forwarded-For headers and bypass IP blocks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:369
msgid "Permanent IP Blocklist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:371
#: includes/class-docs.php:378
#: includes/class-docs.php:596
#: includes/class-docs.php:903
msgid "Empty"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:372
msgid "Bulk list of IPs/CIDRs (one per line, # comments supported) returning immediate 403 Forbidden errors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:373
msgid "Avoid dumping thousands of unmaintained third-party IP feeds here—use WAF + Country Restriction for broad filtering."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:379
msgid "Safelist static office, home, or VPN IPs/CIDRs so trusted team members and monitoring uptime bots bypass login lockouts and rate limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:380
msgid "NEVER add public coffee-shop Wi-Fi, shared cellular gateways, or Cloudflare/CDN proxy IPs into the Allowlist—everyone sharing that IP would bypass security!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:394
msgid "Logins, 2FA, Passkeys & Auth"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:396
msgid "WPEPP Security → Logins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:398
msgid "Full authentication suite organized into 7 sub-tabs: Login Protection, Registration, Passwords, Two-Factor Auth, Passkeys, Custom Login URL, and Auto Login Magic Links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:402
msgid "Custom Login URL & Hide wp-login.php Lockout Warning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:403
msgid "Never enable \"Hide wp-login.php\" until you have already entered, saved, and bookmarked a Custom Login Slug AND excluded that slug from page caching plugins! If locked out, define WPEPP_SAFE_MODE = true in wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:407
msgid "Under Login Protection, verify Login Limiter (default 5 attempts / 15 min) and Auto-Check \"Remember Me\" match your user policy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:408
msgid "Enable Password Policies for new registrations and resets without breaking existing users."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:409
msgid "If masking the login endpoint, set and test Custom Login Slug first, then optionally toggle Hide wp-login.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:410
msgid "Pro users can enforce Role-Based 2FA (TOTP), register Passkeys over HTTPS, and issue temporary time-limited Auto Login links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:414
msgid "Login Limiter (Max Attempts & Lockout Duration)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:416
msgid "On (5 tries / 15 min)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:417
msgid "Temporarily locks out an IP address after repeated wrong passwords (configurable 1–20 attempts, 1–120 minutes). Automatically logs events and triggers lockout alerts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:418
msgid "Do not set Max Attempts to 1–2—normal users mistype passwords and lock themselves out. On Cloudflare, configure Trusted Proxies first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:421
#: build/20.js:1
#: src/pages/Security/LoginProtection.jsx:92
msgid "Auto-Check \"Remember Me\""
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:424
msgid "Pre-selects WordPress's built-in \"Remember Me\" checkbox on wp-login.php so users keep their standard 14-day WordPress auth cookie across browser closes and computer restarts instead of logging in daily."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:425
msgid "Turn this OFF on shared/public kiosk computers or sensitive client environments where closing the browser should strictly end the login session."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:428
msgid "WordPress Hardening (XML-RPC, WP Version, REST User Enumeration)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:430
msgid "All 3 On"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:431
msgid "Blocks xmlrpc.php amplification attacks, strips the WP version generator tag from HTML source, and restricts /wp/v2/users for non-admin requests to stop username harvesting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:432
msgid "Disable \"Disable XML-RPC\" only if you actively rely on Jetpack or legacy mobile/desktop publishing apps. Disable REST User Restriction only if a custom frontend script requires anonymous access to author endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:437
msgid "Default (wp-admin)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:438
msgid "Send users to a custom dashboard or portal URL immediately after successful login."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:439
msgid "Do not point to an access-restricted or 404 page—test the destination URL first, and leave blank on standard admin/WooCommerce sites using role-specific redirects."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:442
msgid "Registration Protection (Rate Limit, Disposable Blocker, Domain Filter, Admin Approval)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:444
msgid "Honeypot On / Others Off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:445
msgid "Limits rapid signups per IP (Free, 1–20 signups / 5–1440 min). Pro adds Disposable Email Blocker, Whitelist/Blacklist Email Domain rules (one domain per line without @), and Require Admin Approval (approve under Users → All Users)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:446
msgid "Never select Email Domain \"Whitelist\" unless you strictly want ONLY those domains (it blocks Gmail/Outlook too!). Avoid Require Admin Approval on instant self-serve eCommerce shops."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:449
msgid "Password Strength & Breach Policy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:451
msgid "Off (Breach Check Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:452
msgid "Enforces min length (6–64, default 12), uppercase+lowercase+number mix, optional special symbol, common weak-list rejection, and Pro k-anonymity check via api.pwnedpasswords.com (only 5 hash chars sent; fails open on outage)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:453
msgid "Do not enforce 20+ char symbol rules on casual WooCommerce customer accounts unless required—excessive friction increases cart/signup abandonment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:456
msgid "Two-Factor Authentication (TOTP App)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:459
msgid "Require 6-digit codes from Google Authenticator, Authy, or Microsoft Authenticator for selected roles, optionally remember trusted devices (Off or 7–90 days), and save one-time Recovery Codes immediately during QR setup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:460
msgid "Do NOT select Subscriber/Customer roles unless your frontend users expect app-based 2FA setup in their profile, and ensure your server clock stays NTP-synced."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:463
msgid "Passkeys (Fingerprint / Face ID / Hardware Key)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:465
msgid "Available on Login"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:466
msgid "Users register WebAuthn device passkeys (\"MacBook Touch ID\", Windows Hello, YubiKey) and click \"Sign in with a passkey\" on wp-login.php with no password required."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:467
msgid "Do NOT attempt passkey registration on plain HTTP staging URLs—browsers enforce HTTPS (or localhost only) for WebAuthn."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:470
msgid "Custom Login URL & Hide wp-login.php"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:473
msgid "Masks wp-login.php behind a clean secret slug (lowercase letters, digits, hyphens—e.g. team-portal) and optionally returns 404 for direct wp-login.php and logged-out wp-admin requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:474
msgid "Do NOT use generic slugs like \"login\" or \"admin\" if bots scan them, and NEVER enable Hide wp-login.php while Custom Login Slug is blank or page caching caches the custom login page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:477
msgid "Auto Login Magic Links"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:479
msgid "On-Demand (3 Free)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:480
msgid "Creates single-click login URLs for any user with optional custom redirect (up to 3 active links Free). Pro removes the cap and adds Expiration (1h–30d), Max Uses (1–100), and Role Restriction."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:481
msgid "Treat magic links as full passwords! NEVER leave \"Never expires\" + unlimited Administrator links sitting in emails or chat logs—always set strict expiration + max uses, and delete immediately after support completes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:495
msgid "Site Access & Geo Gate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:497
msgid "WPEPP Security → Site Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:499
msgid "Whole-site visibility controls across three sub-tabs: Site Access Gate (login/role restriction), Site Password Protection (shared password screen), and Country Restriction (geo-blocking by visitor IP)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:503
msgid "Impact on SEO & Public Visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:504
msgid "Enabling Site Access Gate or Site Password hides your ENTIRE frontend from anonymous users and search engine crawlers (Googlebot). Only use these on client staging sites, private portals, or pre-launch builds—never on active SEO blogs or public eCommerce stores."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:508
msgid "Pick Site Access Gate to require WordPress accounts (All Logged-in Users or Administrators Only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:509
msgid "Or choose Site Password when you want clients to unlock a staging site with a shared password without creating user accounts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:510
msgid "Or configure Country Restriction to hide the site from specific countries (or restrict solely to target regions)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:514
msgid "Site Access Gate (Scope & Logged-Out Action)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:517
msgid "Choose between \"All Logged-in Users (Members Only)\" or \"Administrators Only (manage_options)\". Logged-out guests redirect to login (Free) or see a blurred Glassdoor Login Popup overlay (Pro) with customizable header & message."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:518
msgid "Do not enable on live public stores or WooCommerce APIs/webhooks that expect unauthenticated frontend endpoints unless tested."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:523
msgid "Off (Cookie 7 days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:524
msgid "Requires a global password before showing any frontend page (must enter a password to activate). Customize message, Cookie Duration (1–365 days), and Logged-In User Bypass (Administrators always bypass)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:525
msgid "Avoid using aggressive full-page server/CDN caching (Cloudflare APO, Varnish) without excluding WPEPP unlock cookies—cached HTML may serve either the form to unlocked users or content to locked visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:528
msgid "Country Restriction (Block List vs. Allow List)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:530
msgid "Off (2 Countries Free / Unlimited Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:531
msgid "Resolves country via Cloudflare CF-IPCountry header when present, otherwise queries ipapi.co (sending visitor IP externally; administrators never blocked; fails open on lookup outage). Use Block List to hide from spam-heavy regions or Allow List for geo-locked businesses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:532
msgid "Be VERY careful with \"Allow List\" mode on SEO sites—major search crawlers operate mostly from US/EU datacenters and get blocked if their country is omitted. Remember to configure Trusted Proxies for Cloudflare first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:546
msgid "Hardening & Response Headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:548
msgid "WPEPP Security → Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:550
msgid "Applies server-level filesystem protections, audits permissions on critical files like wp-config.php and .htaccess, manages browser security HTTP headers, and runs live configuration diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:554
msgid "Handle HSTS & Preload With Extreme Care"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:555
msgid "Enabling HSTS tells visitors' browsers to refuse HTTP forever for the max-age window. Enabling \"preload\" marks the domain for hardcoded browser lists (hstspreload.org) which takes months to reverse. NEVER turn on HSTS on HTTP sites, local dev, or domains with non-HTTPS subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:559
msgid "Enable Block PHP in Uploads, Disable Directory Listing, and Disable File Editor under Server Tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:560
msgid "Check the Critical Files table to verify wp-config.php and .htaccess show Protected status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:561
