#: includes/class-docs.php:718
msgid "Controls whether AI training scrapers and AI search/answer engines (OpenAI GPTBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Anthropic ClaudeBot, Google-Extended, CCBot, Bytespider, etc.) may index your pages via robots.txt or active HTTP 403 User-Agent enforcement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:722
msgid "Why This Feature Is OFF by Default (AI Search & Traffic Tradeoff)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:723
msgid "Enabling AI Crawler Blocker stops bots from training on your site, BUT blocking search/citation crawlers (like OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended) also stops ChatGPT, Perplexity, and AI Overviews from recommending or linking to your articles and products! Leave OFF if you want AI discovery traffic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:727
msgid "Decide first whether you want AI visibility/recommendations (leave OFF) or strict anti-scraping protection (turn ON)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:728
msgid "Enable AI Crawler Blocker to automatically append Disallow: / directives for selected bots to WordPress's virtual robots.txt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:729
msgid "Review the 21 known AI bots checklist—for balanced protection, uncheck AI search/citation bots (OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot) while keeping dataset-only scrapers checked."
msgstr ""

