msgid "Global Custom CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:904
msgid "Inject custom CSS rules applying across all plugin front-end outputs (password forms, login screen, member-only template)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:905
msgid "Do not paste general theme header/footer layout CSS here—scope selectors to plugin containers so theme updates never conflict."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:919
msgid "FAQ & Emergency Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:921
msgid "Troubleshooting & Safe Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:923
msgid "Quick answers to common configuration issues plus step-by-step Emergency Safe Mode instructions if a firewall rule, Custom Login URL, or IP block ever locks you out of wp-admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:927
msgid "3 Ways to Trigger Emergency Safe Mode (Instant Bypass)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:928
msgid "Safe Mode temporarily suspends WPEPP firewall checks, login lockouts, custom login hiding, and IP blocks without deactivating your settings. Use any of the three methods below, fix the setting inside wp-admin, and remove the constant/file immediately afterward."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:934
msgid "I forgot my Custom Login URL or got locked out by Hide wp-login.php / IP Block. How do I get back in?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:935
msgid "Trigger Emergency Safe Mode using any method above: add define( 'WPEPP_SAFE_MODE', true ); in wp-config.php, create an empty wp-content/wpepp-safe-mode.txt file via FTP, or run \"wp wpepp safe-mode enable\" via WP-CLI. Visit wp-login.php normally, fix your slug or IP Allowlist, then remove Safe Mode immediately so protection resumes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:938
msgid "Why does WordPress keep asking me to log in frequently after browser restart?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:939
msgid "Go to WPEPP Security → Logins → Login Protection and verify \"Auto-Check Remember Me\" is ON (it is enabled by default so users keep WordPress's normal 14-day cookie). If it is already ON and you still get logged out, verify another security plugin, browser privacy mode, or HTTP/HTTPS cookie mismatch is not clearing cookies on exit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:942
msgid "Why did Login Limiter or Country Restriction lock out normal visitors when using Cloudflare?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:943
msgid "Without Trusted Reverse Proxies configured, WordPress sees Cloudflare's proxy IP instead of each visitor's real IP—causing all visitors to share one rate-limit counter. Open Block Center → IP Lists and click \"1-Click Add Cloudflare IP Ranges\", then click Save Changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:946
msgid "Why is AI Crawler Blocker disabled by default?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:947
msgid "Blocking AI search crawlers (ChatGPT-User, OAI-SearchBot, PerplexityBot) removes your site and products from AI citations and recommendations. WPEPP keeps it OFF by default to protect your AI organic traffic while giving site owners one-click control if strict anti-scraping is desired."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:950
msgid "My Login Form or Site Password page looks unstyled or shows stale locked state after unlocking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:951
msgid "Full-page cache plugins or Cloudflare cache rules may serve old HTML. Clear your cache after styling changes, and ensure your caching plugin excludes wp-login.php, your Custom Login Slug, and requests carrying WPEPP site-password cookies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:954
msgid "If I upgrade to Pro or temporarily deactivate the plugin, will I lose my settings?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-docs.php:955
msgid "No. Deactivating or updating preserves all saved settings, custom designs, and content-lock meta values in WordPress. Data is removed ONLY if you explicitly check Settings → General → Delete Data on Uninstall and then delete the plugin."
msgstr ""

